# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 A ablation_onset 0.2040 93.759 7.3614e+07 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~94 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
2 - first_light 0.2850 91.244 3.3001e+08 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
3 Y first_yield 2.3580 26.928 7.0325e+12 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 30 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 2.3945 25.803 2.0927e+13 stylized  Light rises x8.9 in 0.14 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 26.8 km (93% of m0); split gen 0 at 25.0 km (88% of m0); yield gen 1 at 24.4 km (32% of m0) +2 more. Dust groups supply 20% of the rise and 18% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 2.4180 25.081 3.7569e+13 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x5.3 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 P peak 2.4209 24.989 3.1988e+14 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+0.7 km from the peak of energy deposition (24.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 31.6 km/s).
7 D rolloff 2.4359 24.549 1.0292e+14 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.01 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 98% of v0, 74% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
8 - drag_overtakes_ablation 2.7590 16.603 3.2921e+11 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
9 T tail 2.7613 16.577 3.0677e+11 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
